  "title": "Brenda H NDE 22671",
  "date": "December 21 1982",
  "content": "I had just delivered my eldest daughter. It was December 21, 1982. In the Recovery Room, I became very cold. The nurses gave me seven warming blankets and I was still cold. I was transported back to my original room, with another patient, although I was still freezing. Each time the nurse came in the room I would let her know how very cold it was, but she ignored me. As she left the room for the fourth time, the IV came out my vein and blood was everywhere, on the gown, sheets, and the floor. My roommate called for the nurse, my blood pressure had risen very, very, high. I remember being placed on another stretcher and taken down this well-lit hall. I remember seeing a lot of nurses and Doctors around my bed, with needles and other devices, which they used. All of a sudden I was lifted out of my body to the corner of the ceiling in the Hospital room, as I looked down, I could see my body lifelessly on the table, with tubes, IVs and I could see the Doctors and Nurses all around me calling my name. Brenda, Brenda! I actually heard and saw them; I actually felt the same, without a body. Suddenly I was drawn through the ceiling; I felt nothing, just went through. I saw a very, very bright tunnel. As I moved toward it, closer and closer, all of a sudden, I felt something all over my body. The doctors had injected me with something and I returned to my body on the table, I stayed in ICU for 4 days. After this happened, I took a walk around the Nurses Station. The Nurses who were there that night, mouth flew open -with a sigh they said Mrs. Hines, (I was single at the time), they were astonished, I also heard whispers, we thought she didn't make it, then the Doctor came in my room and said \"We thought you were a goner\".",
